cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Observable Geometry, please cite this software and the GBFs method separately."
title: "Observable Geometry"
version: 0.1.3-dev.1
authors:
  - family-names: Tyagi
    given-names: Tranav
license: BSD-3-Clause
abstract: >-
  Auditable software for reproducing a bounded GBFs workflow and measuring
  nominal, covariance-whitened similarity between candidate EEG source
  signatures under a declared participant-specific forward model. The
  diagnostic does not establish physiological source recovery or calibrated
  localization uncertainty.
date-released: 2026-10-30
repository-code: "https://github.com/tranav4464/observable-geometry"
